#
# Once a day: the Web Application Firewall's audit and error logs' day files older than OPNsense keeps
# its own logs (System: Settings: Logging, Preserve logs, 31 days by default) taken away (setup.py
# prune). With none there it lists an empty directory and exits; it reads config.xml once and contacts
# no one. In /usr/local/etc/cron.d, as the family's other plugins: OPNsense writes its own crontab again
# from its own jobs.

17 4 * * * root /usr/local/opnsense/scripts/modsecurity/setup.py prune > /dev/null 2>&1
